# Directories (need /* suffix for zip -x@ to exclude recursively)
.git/*
.github/*
.claude/*
node_modules/*

# Development files
.DS_Store
.gitignore
.distignore
.gitattributes
.editorconfig
.gitkeep
phpcs.xml
phpcs.xml.dist
composer.json
composer.lock
/package.json
/package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# Documentation and scripts
# Kept as a guard, not a description: there is no docs/ or designs/ directory
# here any more. Planning documents and design mockups live in the private
# imagewize.com repo under docs/aludra/ and designs/aludra/ (see CLAUDE.md).
# These entries stay so that a stray file re-added here never reaches a zip.
docs/*
designs/
designs/*
bin/*
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
CONTRIBUTING.md
README.md
*.sh
create-pr.sh

# Block tooling. blocks/*/src/* and blocks/*/package.json deliberately DO ship:
# every file under blocks/*/build/ is webpack output, and WordPress.org
# guideline 4 requires the human-readable source of compiled JS/CSS to ship
# alongside it. The src trees are ~18k lines / ~1MB and the package.json files
# ~120KB, negligible in a 3MB dist; the per-block lockfiles are 14MB, so those
# stay out.
#
# Why the root entries above are written `/package.json` and not `package.json`:
# the two release paths use different exclude dialects. create-release.yml runs
# `zip -x@`, which matches whole paths, but plugin-check.yml and wp-ops
# rsync-package-to-site run rsync's --exclude-from, where a pattern with no
# slash matches a *basename at any depth* — so a bare `package.json` silently
# took all 30 blocks/*/package.json with it. A leading slash anchors to the
# transfer root in rsync and is still matched by zip, so it is correct in both.
# Verified empirically against both tools; keep any new root-only entry anchored.
blocks/*/node_modules/*
blocks/*/package-lock.json
blocks/*/.gitignore
blocks/*/.npmrc
blocks/*/eslint.config.js
blocks/*/.editorconfig

